      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C29"],
      "claim": "Rotigotine has ~5% absolute oral bioavailability due to phenolic first-pass conjugation; the query contains only an aliphatic hydroxyl and no phenolic/catechol moiety, so this clearance mechanism is absent.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is the galantamine scaffold: a compact tertiary-amine alkaloid with an aliphatic hydroxyl and no carbamate, quaternary ammonium, phenolic/catechol, ketone, or large polyphenolic moieties. The retrieved low-bioavailability records are direct human F measurements, but their low F is attributable to specific structural liabilities absent in the query; therefore the high transfer scores do not mechanistically translate. The query's favorable permeability and metabolic stability profile support F >= 20%.",
